So when you go to the past, you go to the same screen, you plant the seed.

00:16:41.060 --> 00:16:44.160
When you come back to the present, now there's a tree there pretty cool.

00:16:44.160 --> 00:16:49.040
Like, you know, good representation, very similar to Chrono Trigger where like, if you open

00:16:49.040 --> 00:16:56.200
a chest and then, um, and then go in, if you open a chest in the past and then go back to

00:16:56.200 --> 00:16:57.780
the present, like the chest is already open.

00:16:57.780 --> 00:17:02.060
So you kind of spoiled, uh, the reward cause it's already been opened.

00:17:02.160 --> 00:17:06.660
Whereas if you do it properly, you can open up the chest several times and get several different

00:17:06.660 --> 00:17:12.040
rewards. The novelty of the time travel though is a little less interesting here.

00:17:12.480 --> 00:17:16.900
One, because it's, it's very forcibly done where you have to, in order to progress, you

00:17:16.900 --> 00:17:22.400
have to, um, like jump just to the past, do what you do in the past, go back to the present,

00:17:22.420 --> 00:17:29.100
so on and so forth. But also the NPCs kind of seem to be aware of the time gates and the ability of time travel

00:17:29.100 --> 00:17:35.940
and like explaining to, to the player, but also to you, the player very clearly what to

00:17:35.940 --> 00:17:37.100
do with time travel.

00:17:37.440 --> 00:17:40.820
Like, um, the character, they're like Farouk was here 50 years ago.

00:17:41.020 --> 00:17:43.020
If you go there, you'll meet him.

00:17:43.120 --> 00:17:46.440
It's like, what the hell does that, like, you know, like if you knew about time travel,

00:17:46.500 --> 00:17:48.840
like why don't you go back in time and meet him?

00:17:48.980 --> 00:17:50.160
Like what is, what is that about?

00:17:50.400 --> 00:17:57.380
Yeah. I was very thrown off just by their use of there instead of like, yeah, if you were around

00:17:57.380 --> 00:18:00.060
back then, then you'd have seen him.

00:18:00.060 --> 00:18:06.180
Um, it, it very much like everyone here is in on it, but you, and why hasn't anybody

00:18:06.180 --> 00:18:07.660
else been time traveling?

00:18:08.040 --> 00:18:09.960
Like, it, it's weird.

00:18:11.460 --> 00:18:16.300
Yeah. I mean, and the time travel is very, like you said, very like story driven.

00:18:16.560 --> 00:18:20.400
It's, it, it doesn't feel like it's a tool that you have that you can utilize in some

00:18:20.400 --> 00:18:21.360
unique and interesting way.

00:18:21.460 --> 00:18:23.320
It's like, no, this is when the story wants you to time travel.

00:18:23.600 --> 00:18:27.000
Like you do it then everything is in place the way that it's supposed to be.

00:18:27.000 --> 00:18:29.980
You change something that you're supposed to change and you leave.

00:18:30.300 --> 00:18:34.020
Not that like I was expecting like, oh, an NES game is going to be like, I mean, even

00:18:34.020 --> 00:18:36.400
Chrono Trigger to some extent has a lot of that.

00:18:36.520 --> 00:18:41.540
And then it has some other stuff that like is a little more, um, you have a little more

00:18:41.540 --> 00:18:44.640
agency with, but like, yeah, I definitely wasn't expecting it to be more like that, but

00:18:44.640 --> 00:18:48.560
yeah, I just don't want anyone to think like, oh my God, you can go back and, you know,

00:18:48.660 --> 00:18:51.200
you can go back and kill the bad guy as a baby.

00:18:51.880 --> 00:18:53.300
No, you can't do shit like that.

00:18:54.400 --> 00:18:57.260
And you only go like 500 years into the past.

00:18:57.540 --> 00:19:02.600
So why do the maps change so much, uh, between 500 years?

00:19:02.720 --> 00:19:08.360
Like I'm not talking about like the placement of towns or even just like enemy enemies or

00:19:08.360 --> 00:19:11.340
stuff. I'm talking about like the actual desert turning into a forest.

00:19:11.500 --> 00:19:15.400
Yeah. A desert turning into a forest, but also like not even, it's not one to one, the same

00:19:15.400 --> 00:19:20.780
screens. So it's not even like if you remember where you were in the present, when you go to the

00:19:20.780 --> 00:19:24.160
past, it'll be like the same layout, but oh, these things have changed.

00:19:24.340 --> 00:19:25.620
You won't really notice.

00:19:25.820 --> 00:19:30.960
Like, it's not like the screen to your right from the time gate is exactly the same in the

00:19:30.960 --> 00:19:32.260
past or in the present.

00:19:32.260 --> 00:19:39.540
It's like even the world itself like has these life altering earthquakes that change the actual

00:19:39.540 --> 00:19:40.480
geography. Yeah.

00:19:40.620 --> 00:19:46.460
At least one is mentioned by like the townspeople, like in the first world, it's like, oh, you

00:19:46.460 --> 00:19:50.180
know, it's really too bad that that one city fell into the sea.

00:19:51.120 --> 00:19:57.880
And like, so I guess you could imagine that some cataclysm struck and changed the geography

00:19:57.880 --> 00:19:58.760
and the environment.

00:19:59.140 --> 00:20:06.920
But, uh, for it to be like everywhere, uh, with this kind of change, it's, it's hard to,

00:20:07.080 --> 00:20:08.020
hard to believe.

00:20:08.620 --> 00:20:13.260
Yeah. And regardless of the story implications of that, it does feel like, uh, it's just such

00:20:13.260 --> 00:20:16.720
a missed opportunity because there's something really cool about revisiting the exact same

00:20:16.720 --> 00:20:18.880
landscape with new stuff in it.

00:20:18.940 --> 00:20:21.660
Like I know where I am, but now I want to see what it's like in the past.

00:20:21.680 --> 00:20:24.060
Like, oh, now I bet this guy's in this spot.

00:20:24.220 --> 00:20:27.960
But if it's not the same spot anymore, then it doesn't really feel like you've traveled

00:20:27.960 --> 00:20:30.400
to the past and you're looking at like a past version of it.

00:20:30.480 --> 00:20:31.880
It just feels like you're on a different map.

00:20:33.260 --> 00:20:35.260
I thought that sometimes it did it okay.

00:20:35.380 --> 00:20:39.960
Like with that sinking city, you can go back to, I think it's roughly where that sinking

00:20:39.960 --> 00:20:41.340
city is in the past.

00:20:41.340 --> 00:20:45.080
When you go there in the present, you can like go underwater and it's like a city of

00:20:45.080 --> 00:20:46.120
mermaids. Yeah.

00:20:46.160 --> 00:20:53.460
Like that's cool. But yeah, it is, it is missing out on the opportunity to like make you go back in time or forward

00:20:53.460 --> 00:20:55.220
in time or whatever and be like, oh, I know this map.

00:20:55.920 --> 00:20:58.120
I just don't know what I'm, what I'm going to run into now.

00:20:58.380 --> 00:21:04.460
Right. And it's a pretty, you know, we were saying that these are level based missions and stuff,

00:21:04.480 --> 00:21:10.460
but it's a pretty expansive game just in terms of what you'll do in the levels and what you'll

00:21:10.460 --> 00:21:12.100
find and what you need to be doing.

00:21:12.100 --> 00:21:18.980
So the manual is very surprising because it's actually, it's like 40 something pages and

00:21:18.980 --> 00:21:19.960
it's pretty in depth.

00:21:20.140 --> 00:21:21.200
It's not a strategy guide.

00:21:21.360 --> 00:21:25.480
It doesn't give you like maps or tell you like starting the game, here's what you need to

00:21:25.480 --> 00:21:30.360
do and stuff. But it really is a good lay of the land in terms of everything that you can do in this

00:21:30.360 --> 00:21:32.560
game. I don't know if you guys looked at that or not.

00:21:32.660 --> 00:21:38.700
It really is just an actual manual, very similar to like board games that give instructions

00:21:38.700 --> 00:21:40.840
about like every single thing that you can do.

00:21:40.980 --> 00:21:45.420
And then you just like. You're like, well, maybe we need to play the game a little bit to understand the rules.

00:21:45.580 --> 00:21:47.140
That happens to me a lot in board games.

00:21:47.260 --> 00:21:48.820
It's very similar with this.

00:21:49.320 --> 00:21:54.280
How did you guys make just getting around and figuring out what to do in the game?

00:21:54.420 --> 00:22:00.120
Was it, was it something where the NPCs were very helpful in giving fetch quests that were

00:22:00.120 --> 00:22:01.680
very obvious about your next steps?

00:22:01.820 --> 00:22:04.780
Or did you find any obtuseness to it?

00:22:05.340 --> 00:22:07.000
I, I think so.

00:22:07.000 --> 00:22:11.360
So usually I will, I will read the manual before I play these games.

00:22:11.600 --> 00:22:13.660
It's, it's kind of rare when I don't do it.

00:22:13.900 --> 00:22:21.140
Um, this time I took a look at it, saw the length, skimmed the first few pages and it was

00:22:21.140 --> 00:22:23.660
just like, I, I can't, I'm just going to play the game.

00:22:23.660 --> 00:22:30.140
Um, and it actually turned out to be pretty easy, but not, not like easy at like the most

00:22:30.140 --> 00:22:36.020
extreme cases, but unlike a lot of games that we played, this one kind of holds your hand

00:22:36.020 --> 00:22:42.940
to some extent. And like you, you can just figure out what a lot of the mechanics of this game are just

00:22:42.940 --> 00:22:43.820
by playing it.

00:22:44.180 --> 00:22:53.360
And, um, like for example, when you enter a screen with a hidden door, your cat will just

00:22:53.360 --> 00:22:57.600
say like, Hey, use that thing and something will happen.

00:22:57.600 --> 00:23:00.380
And so you do when it does.

00:23:01.060 --> 00:23:07.900
So it's not as obscure as I was expecting without any manual knowledge.

00:23:08.520 --> 00:23:09.500
Yeah. I noticed that too.

00:23:09.620 --> 00:23:14.500
I mean, I would say that it's, it is some, it does fall somewhere in the middle of like

00:23:14.500 --> 00:23:19.200
the best and worst cases of this that we've had so far where like there were times where

00:23:19.200 --> 00:23:20.060
I didn't know what to do.

00:23:20.220 --> 00:23:24.160
And then there were other times where I mean, gratefully, what was, you know, what was that

00:23:24.160 --> 00:23:25.400
cat lady's name?

00:23:26.000 --> 00:23:27.020
Caronia or Caronia?

00:23:27.020 --> 00:23:32.360
Caronia. Um, she would like, when you go somewhere, she kind of like says, talk to the townspeople.

