00:23:41.500 --> 00:23:42.420
I bet something's here.

00:23:42.580 --> 00:23:47.780
And it's like, it felt like a solution to that whole thing of like, oh, there's like a

00:23:47.780 --> 00:23:51.600
random spot that we would never guess that you have to do one specific thing to open

00:23:51.600 --> 00:23:54.060
up a door. Like it felt like a solution to that.

00:23:54.060 --> 00:23:59.620
But also I noticed that if you let her as your companion die in battle, then you don't

00:23:59.620 --> 00:24:00.560
get those hints anymore.

00:24:00.700 --> 00:24:07.160
Oh, that kind of felt like a cool, like it made her more than just like, um, either a

00:24:07.160 --> 00:24:13.000
tutorial person or a companion that just fights in battles with you.

00:24:13.000 --> 00:24:15.820
Like it made it like, oh, she's, she's living and breathing in this world.

00:24:15.920 --> 00:24:19.400
And like, Hey, if she dies in a battle, she's not going to do the tutorial thing for you.

00:24:20.240 --> 00:24:22.100
That's pretty cool. I actually didn't know that.

00:24:22.480 --> 00:24:28.940
Yeah. And it both like gave you a little bit of, um, agency, but also like agency to decide

00:24:28.940 --> 00:24:33.440
when you want your hand to be held or like decide how important that is to you when like

