Zelda style. You swing your sword or use your rod and, um, fight these, uh, and fight the enemies on screen.

00:26:14.100 --> 00:26:19.840
They randomly spawn in on the, on the particular screen that you're on, or they don't, it's not

00:26:19.840 --> 00:26:22.580
guaranteed. So you can just kind of keep shuffling back and forth between.

00:26:22.580 --> 00:26:25.780
And then when you deal with all of them, they don't just continuously spawn.

00:26:25.920 --> 00:26:26.780
That's it for that.

00:26:26.940 --> 00:26:28.440
And then you have to continue to move on.

00:26:29.260 --> 00:26:34.440
Interestingly though, just for the like ARPG portion of the game, I found it to be like,

00:26:35.700 --> 00:26:41.840
I don't want to say like too simple or whatever, but compared to the turn-based combat, which

00:26:41.840 --> 00:26:42.900
gives a lot more options.

